Magnetic pad budget. To achieve 0.5 N at 0.5 m would require ~120 A m² per pad, infeasible within mass constraints. We therefore employ the keeper scaffold, which carries distributed stationary electromagnets generating a background dipole field of ~80 A m² within the capture volume. The tile permanent magnets then need only ~24 A m² for fine‑locking at contact, requiring 0.7 kg per hybrid pad, for a total of 4.2 kg—feasible.

4.3 Other Building Blocks

Truss Node. 4 kg, cubic, six A‑Tile‑compatible docking faces, internal power and data bus.

Truss Strut. Telescopic CFRP tube, 2 m extended, 2 kg, providing 10⁴ N m rad⁻¹ bending stiffness when locked.

Propellant Tank Module (PTM). 12 U, 22 kg wet (10 kg ASCENT propellant), tile‑grade GNC, RAFTI interface.

Keeper Scaffold. Inflatable Kevlar mesh torus, 50 m major diameter, 5 kg. Distributed electromagnets are powered by thin‑film amorphous‑silicon solar cells laminated on the torus surface (~400 m², ~40 kW raw generation). EM array draws ~2 kW peak during active docking. Jettisoned after frame closure.

Welding E‑Walker. 12 U CubeSat with electron‑beam welding head (ThinkOrbital‑heritage) and short‑range robotic arm for positioning and fiducial alignment. Truss nodes carry retro‑reflective fiducials for ±2 mm positioning accuracy. A degraded‑mode procedure exists: if both the primary and the cold‑spare E‑Walkers fail, the truss operates on latched/magnetic joints alone (factor 10 stiffness reduction, still within structural margins for uncrewed operation). Crew perform a manual bolt‑tightening EVA after ingress to recover full stiffness.

4.4 Airtightness Strategy

Two parallel development paths are maintained, to be down‑selected after 24‑month thermal‑vacuum and MMOD ground testing.

Criterion Path A: Sealed Tile Habitat Path B: Exoskeleton + Bladder
Concept Compressible Viton gaskets on all six tile edges; EM latches provide 200 N pre‑load per edge; leak rate <10⁻⁶ sccs Thin‑walled (0.3 mm) Kevlar‑reinforced polyurethane bladder deployed inside the assembled tile shell
